WEBVTT

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:33.690
S- Sara-san! What can I do to-

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.460
Sara-san... What do I do now?

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.510
You did what?! You idiot!

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:47.210
You're always causing trouble
every chance you get!

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.380
--I'm sorry...
--So, what's Gutsy Girl doing?!

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.480
It looks like she's going into town,

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.650
but she doesn't have her Daytracer...

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:57.720
Quit crying and come here, too!

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.190
Let's call the others
and have everyone look for it!

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.760
Understood!

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.830
Yeah. Carris here. Say what?!

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.800
Emily disappeared?!

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.030
Gutsy Girl's missing, too!
She's out looking for Emily!

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:13.670
--Eh?!
--Listen! Find her at all costs!

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:17.270
--Which one?!
--Don't be dumb! Both, obviously!

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:20.580
She's headed for a waste
collection point in the city!

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.410
Everyone split up and check
every last one! Understood?!

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:25.570
Understood!

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:32.020
Please, Emily... Be all right!

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:37.180
Gall Space Supply Depot

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.940
H-hey, you! Get out of here!

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.210
--Emily!
--It's dangerous! Get away!

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.480
Emily!

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.590
--Stop!
--Let go! Let go of me!

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:05.090
Emily's- Emily's getting away!

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:08.060
--Emily!
--Sara!

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:11.430
Look closer! That's not Emily!

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.600
This isn't like you.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.570
I heard about Emily.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.640
Emily! I have to find her!

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.840
Just calm down!

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.980
You're not going to find her
by running around recklessly!

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.350
--But-
--Don't worry.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.680
I'll find her for you.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:37.690
I lived here until I went to Basion.
So I know a little about the place.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:41.180
Plus I have some connections.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.560
Welcome! How may I help-

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.470
Get Donny!

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.140
I mean, get Donald Radofrics!
Right away!

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.540
Chief Administrator Radofrics?
May I ask why you-

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.480
It's an emergency!

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.440
Just tell him Carris is here
and he'll understand!

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.110
--B-but...
--Umm, Carris...

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:02.620
Just call him here! I'm his...

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:04.850
--Big Brother?
--Eh?

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.120
Chief Administrator!

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.360
Brother... Brother!

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.160
It is you, Big Brother!

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.060
--"Big Brother"?
--Big Brother!

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.550
I've missed you!

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:19.630
--He's your younger brother?
--Yeah...

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.770
But now he's older than me,

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:26.270
because of all my
sub-light speed travel.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.540
As Chief Satellite Administrator,

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.340
he has full knowledge of
everything that comes in here.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:34.610
Don't worry. We'll know soon.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.550
Plus, everyone else is out
looking for her, too.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.220
Eh? "Everyone"?

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.590
--Oh, whoops!
--You idiot!

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:46.060
If you found her, why didn't
you tell us right away?!

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:48.390
Sara-san! What are you doing?!

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:51.230
You could have at least
talked to us about this!

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.070
Do you have any idea
how worried we were?!

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:54.670
S-sorry...

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:58.070
Besides, what do you think
everything so far has-

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.410
Lavinia! Hold her back, will you?!

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:02.640
R-right!

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.680
--Hey!
--Listen, Gutsy Girl.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.020
Don't worry about a thing!
We're right behind you!

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.820
T-thank you...

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.220
Alright, we'll look around, too.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.860
We're counting on you guys!
Over and out!

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.260
Well, then. How about some food?

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.360
You haven't eaten since morning, right?

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.660
Eh? But...

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.030
Then it's decided!

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:30.370
I know this one restaurant. Let's go!

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.530
Wait...

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:38.510
Gall is far from the Neutral Zone,
so the civilians have a lot of say.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.780
So it's like the very
definition of peace here.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:45.220
And there are lots of carefree
people like me as a result.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.130
It's just like in the old days...

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:58.160
Hiya! What'll it be?

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.930
Let's see...

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:01.630
Carris?

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:05.570
It is you, Carris! Wow!
How many years has it been?!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:09.580
Eh? You don't mean... Janet?!

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.680
"Skinny as a twig" Janet?!

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:15.410
You're so lucky! You're still young!

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.320
Not to mention getting
hitched at such a young age!

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:21.050
Hitched?

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.020
Hold on, now, Janet! It's not like that!

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.460
You don't need to pretend!

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:28.430
He's a bashful daddy, isn't he?

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.450
"Daddy"?

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:35.170
She's a real cute kid!

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.360
Whose looks did she get?

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.970
Is upstairs open?

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.850
We're looking up info on Sara, right?

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:56.290
Then why aren't we doing it
from a military facility?

00:05:56.290 --> 00:06:01.160
I don't like how strict everything is.
All those restrictions and stuff...

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.560
Alright! We're in!

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.860
Now, then. This is where
our real work begins.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:12.640
This is all Sara's bio-data?

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.640
I'm checking it against
the data Joint HQ has

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.740
on hundreds of billions of people.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:19.580
There's no other way to narrow
her down to one person.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:24.420
I guess. But it sounds like
it'll take lots of time.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:26.480
Here you go!

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.660
What's your name?

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.120
Do you know where you live?

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:37.400
She must be lost...

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:41.700
Let's take her to the
Administration Bureau after we eat.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.470
What's wrong?!

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:44.990
Water! Water!

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.100
Are you okay?

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:55.170
Wait!

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.280
Look out!

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:58.880
Sara!

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:08.830
Are you okay? You're not hurt, are you?

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.600
Thank you.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:13.270
Don't suddenly dash off anymore, okay?

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.670
--Are you okay?
--Yes.

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:18.330
Wait!

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:40.160
Let's see... Where should we start?

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.560
There are eight places
on this floor alone...

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.560
Hey, Ermy!
What's happening on your end?!

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.230
No luck! On our way
to the next candidate!

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:51.270
--How about you, Dickon?!
--I got nothin' here.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.800
I don't see any dolls that look like her.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:07.920
I see. Yeah.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:11.590
Alright. Please keep at it, then.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.730
Sounds like it'll take
Donny a little more time.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:17.400
--Oh...
--Don't worry!

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.700
It sounds like they've
really narrowed it down now!

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.790
Plus Lottie and the others
are on their way here.

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:27.410
She has such innocence, doesn't she?

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.340
She sure does.

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:31.380
You've had a pretty rough day.

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:33.280
You've done a lot of
hard work today yourself.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:36.020
No, I actually had a pretty good time!

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:38.550
I think you'll make a good dad someday.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:41.050
I think you'll make an even better mom.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:43.890
--Eh?
--No, uhh...

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.460
The degaussing.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:55.500
Magnetic energy's always
built up easily in this city.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:59.540
Left unchecked, it'll turn
electronics into useless junk.

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:01.530
Which is why...

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.450
Wow!

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:14.450
...they expel the built-up magnetic
energy every 24 hours, like so.

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:19.590
Oh, yeah! Here, you go!
A present, for your dear friend!

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:23.400
--For Emily?
--Yeah, it's a dress.

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.600
She might be dirty from
all the garbage and stuff,

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.330
so I figured she might
need new clothes.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.170
Thank you...

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:35.010
Why?

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:39.180
Why is everyone always...

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.750
Why is everyone always
looking out so much for me?

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.680
What're you talking about?
We're friends.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.750
But-

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:51.420
Quit talking about yourself like that.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:55.890
Besides, every time I saw
you looking lonely somewhere,

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:59.200
I wished there was something
I could do for you.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.930
Was doing this a bother, though?

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:04.200
Not at all...

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.230
That's good.

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:17.680
Sara...

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:25.490
Dammit, Donny! You have no tact!

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:28.390
Yeah, it's me! Eh? What?

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:52.280
Eh? What? The degaussing hasn't
ended here yet! I can't hear you!

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.410
Oh, you're awake?

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:57.420
What is it?

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:06.690
What is it?
Did you find something else?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:10.240
--Wait...
--Section S-35?

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:14.840
Oh, the one with the weird-
shaped neon light?! Great!

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.840
Sara! Sara?

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:21.580
Hold on, Big Brother!
Stay away from there for now!

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:27.050
We've just got word something's
happened in the outer wall there!

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:29.250
Huh? What do you mean, "something"?!

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.290
Just be careful! I'll contact you later!

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.280
--Bye!
--Hey! Donny!

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:42.130
What the- Emergency orders
to return to ship?!

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.170
An unregistered unit?!

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:50.880
The local garrison has requested
we send Strains to conduct recon.

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:54.310
I've ordered all the cadets
who've left to return to ship.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:57.820
They've already dispersed all
available manpower to patrol the ports.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.090
So, given as we're the closest...

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:02.960
--...they dropped the work into our laps.
--So it would seem.

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:06.660
Urgh! You're useless! I told you
not to take your eyes off her!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.890
S-sorry...

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:11.560
S-35, was it?! I'll go there!

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:13.970
You guys head back
and get ready to move out!

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:17.000
--Jessie! You're in charge!
--Understood!

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.100
I'm coming, too!

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:22.240
You idiot! We can't split
our forces up any more!

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:23.940
Let's go, Carris.

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:26.350
Yeah... Yeah!

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:31.150
Jessie! This is my hometown!
Follow me, I know a shortcut!

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:32.810
Understood!

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.000
A waste-collection point?!

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.930
Why would she come
to a place like this?!

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:53.070
--Just a little bit more...
--It really did take a long time...

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:55.670
By the way, what about
the orders to return to ship?

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.680
I'm almost done,
so just ignore it for now.

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:01.080
I'm sure it's no big deal, anyway...

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:02.650
Where's Lavinia?

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:07.390
She's with Lottie. She said they're
looking for Emily with Sara.

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:09.620
Then I should've gone, too!

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:14.530
That worried? A boy in love
sure has it tough!

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:16.430
Yeah, I'm worried!
Got a problem with that?!

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:20.300
That's enough pointless banter.
Here is the situation.

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:24.300
The signal of an unidentified
unit disappeared near Sector S-35.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:25.470
That's-

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:29.370
The recent degaussing has jammed
the various sensors out there.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.710
Exercise extreme caution.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.160
We're only here for reconnaissance!
Don't get needlessly close!

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.150
Got that, everyone?!

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:56.260
Where did she go?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.850
There she is!

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:35.130
Sara!

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:38.210
Emily?!

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:42.910
Emily!

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:47.410
Thank goodness! Thank goodness!

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:55.230
That's the tenth reminder
to return to ship!

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:59.230
Forget it! This is more important!

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:01.300
Yes, here we go!

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:04.600
You're safe now, Emily...

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:07.110
I'm so sorry I left you all alone...

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:14.180
No, that's okay! After all,
I had faith you'd find me again!

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:18.320
It was pitch dark all that time...
There was no one there...

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:23.260
I was scared... and cold...
and lonely...

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:26.320
But then you found me, Sara...

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:31.800
You gave me a name.
You talked to me everyday...

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:35.030
So I wasn't lonely anymore...

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:40.310
What... are you saying?
Who are you?

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:41.770
Emily...

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:45.440
I'm Emily, Sara...

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:48.880
Sara... Werec.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:51.950
We're almost there!
Be careful, everyone!

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:53.050
Carris?

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:57.460
Sara might be in the area!
I can't be easygoing about this!

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:58.720
Eh?!

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:02.260
Found 'em!

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:05.900
I've located TUMORs!
Are they the unidentified units?!

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:09.200
I'm worried about Sara!
Let's take care of these, Dickon!

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.870
Wait!

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:15.710
What are you talking about? Emily is-

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:20.410
This girl is me. I've been looking
for her for a long, long time.

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:23.520
I missed her... It was lonely...

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:26.590
For her, and for me...

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:29.820
But you were nice to me...

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:31.920
So I came to see you...

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.890
Who are you?

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.720
Emily.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.340
I-it can't be...

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:53.110
For now, let's draw them out of here!

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.580
Okay!

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:01.810
That's it! Keep following me!

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:08.890
What is that?! A hole?!

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:16.720
Crap! They're falling!

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:36.550
What the hell's going on?!
Where's Sara?!

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:47.000
Brother...

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:57.780
She's that girl?!

00:17:57.780 --> 00:17:59.810
Brother! Wait!

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:01.580
What is this all about?!

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:03.100
Answer me!

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:08.020
Don't bother with me.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:12.190
Forget about me and this girl.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.290
There is something I've decided to do.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:17.460
No matter what it takes.

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:19.130
So...

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:21.160
...stay out of my way!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.000
The Gloire!

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:29.540
That's Ralph Werec's!

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:32.610
Why is he here?!

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:35.050
I won't show mercy to anyone
who gets in my way.

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:38.520
Not even to you, Sara!

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:40.220
Wait! Wait!

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.250
Answer me!

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:46.290
What happened to you?!
Why are you doing this?!

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:47.920
Wait!

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:53.160
Wait! Wait!

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:54.890
Brother!

00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:07.410
What did you just say?

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:10.380
What the hell did you just say?!

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:14.850
That should be most of 'em!

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:18.590
Yeah. But I'm concerned
about that hole earlier!

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:21.090
Geez! What a worrywart!

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:23.400
Don't get needlessly close, Carris!

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.990
This is no time for that!

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:30.030
What?!

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:34.130
Carris!

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:50.890
Dickon! Dickon! Are you alive?!

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:53.590
Jessie! Carris is- Carris is-

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:57.430
What is it?! What happened?!
What flew off just now?!

00:19:57.430 --> 00:19:59.560
Report!

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:19.220
Answer me...

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:23.760
What the hell do you mean he-
Ralph Werec- is your brother?!

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:26.120
Answer me, Sara!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.460
Answer me!

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:32.980
Her heart seethes with
the desire for revenge.

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:35.750
A bloodthirsty gun barrel is pointed.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:39.560
On the next Soukou no Strain:
"Like Looking at Myself"

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:42.150
But... I can't die.
